    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "q": "Who approves spending above my limit?",
      "a": "Ravi Campbell, the CFO, for anything over USD 2,000. Gifts over USD 250 go to Dana.",
      "tag": "Money",
      "see": "handover-decide"
    },
    {
      "q": "What do I do if Dana's flight is cancelled?",
      "a": "Rebook the next flight in the same class through the travel desk first, then tell her. Don't wait for approval.",
      "tag": "If this happens",
      "see": "handover-knowledge"
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I book time with the board chair?",
      "a": "No. Requests go through Dana, using the chair's meeting request template.",
      "tag": "People",
      "see": "handover-people"
    },
    {
      "q": "Where are the passwords?",
      "a": "In the Exec vault in the company password manager. IT adds you on day one.",
      "tag": "Access",
      "see": "handover-access"
    },
    { "q": "Until when can I ask Priya?", "a": "Until 27 November, weekdays 10:00 to 12:00, on WhatsApp.", "tag": "People" }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "how-dana-works",
      "title": "How Dana works",
      "body": "- Mornings are for thinking: no meetings before 10:00 unless she asks.\n- She reads WhatsApp, not email, after 18:00.\n- Fridays after 15:00 are meeting-free.\n\n> The full principal profile is in the documents list. Dana confirmed it with one correction."
    },
    {
      "id": "confidentiality",
      "title": "Confidentiality",
      "body": "- Board papers go through the portal only, never as email attachments.\n- The personal calendar is for Dana, Sam and you. Nobody else sees it.\n\n!> Never forward a board pack, even internally."
    },
    {
      "id": "handover-role",
      "title": "About the role",
      "body": "Runs Dana Whitfield's desk so she can spend her time on the business: her diary, correspondence, travel, expenses and the board calendar. The role is the first point of contact for anyone who needs the CEO.\n\n| About the role | Details |\n|---|---|\n| Organisation | Example Holdings |\n| Location | Head office, in person |\n| Hours | Weekdays 8:00 to 5:00, with some evening events |\n| Travel | Rarely: Dana travels, and the desk runs from the office |\n| Manages | No direct reports. Books the company driver for Dana |\n\n### Skills and experience the work calls for\n\n- Running a senior executive's diary, inbox and travel\n- Discretion with board papers and personal information\n- Accurate expense claims and card reconciliations\n- Clear, polite writing to board members and outside guests\n\n### What good looks like\n\n- Expense claims reach Finance by Thursday noon every week\n- Board packs go out through the portal on time, never by email\n- Dana agrees the next week's diary every Friday"
    },
    {
      "id": "handover-as-needed",
      "title": "Jobs done as needed",
      "body": "| Job | When | Area | Details |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Answer meeting requests for Dana | When a request comes in | Diary and correspondence | Accept or decline internal requests yourself. Requests to the board chair go through Dana, using the template in the documents list. |\n| Book Dana's travel, and rebook when a trip changes | When Dana plans a trip | Travel | Through the Northstar Travel desk. Book alone up to USD 2,000; above that, check with Ravi Campbell first. |\n| Draft visa invitation letters for overseas guests | When an overseas guest is invited | Travel | TODO: the wording Priya used, and who signs them |"
    },
    {
      "id": "handover-people",
      "title": "People",
      "body": "| Name | Role | Contact |\n|---|---|---|\n| Priya Nair | Outgoing assistant, Owner | priya.nair@example.com until 25 September |\n| Marcus Hale | Incoming assistant | marcus.hale@example.com |\n| Dana Whitfield | Principal | Through her own WhatsApp and email; she never opens the handover tool |\n| Helen Ortiz | Facilitator | HR business partner, helen.ortiz@example.com |\n\n### People to know\n\n| Name | Who they are | When to involve them | Contact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Ravi Campbell | Chief financial officer | Approves spend above the limits on the who-decides board, and the quarterly board budget. | Ext. 2210, or his assistant Kim |\n| Joy Lindo | Company secretary | Board calendar, board packs and minutes. Agree the pack timetable with her a month before each board meeting. | Ext. 2240 |\n| Elaine Brooks | Chair of the board | Only through Dana. Never book time with her directly; send requests with the template in the documents list. | Through her office manager, details in the protected contacts file |\n| Andre Clarke | Company driver | Airport runs and evening events. Give him flight numbers, not just times. | Mobile in the shared contacts |\n| Northstar Travel desk | The company's travel agency | Flights, hotels and rebooking when a trip changes. They hold Dana's travel preferences. | travel desk email in the booking portal |\n| Sam Whitfield | Dana's partner | Family dates go in the personal calendar. Check it before accepting anything in the evening or at weekends. | In the protected contacts file |"
    },
    {
      "id": "handover-access",
      "title": "Systems and documents",
      "body": "| System | Used for | Credential kept in | Access from | Access check |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Diary (Outlook) | Dana's work diary, with delegate access | Company single sign-on; no separate password | IT service desk, approved by Dana | Opens: pass; Can create: pass; Right level: pass |\n| Board portal | Board packs, minutes and the board calendar | Exec vault in the password manager, Board folder | TODO: confirm whether Joy or IT grants editor access | Opens: pass; Right level: pass |\n| Expenses tool | Submitting Dana's claims | Company single sign-on | Finance, Ravi Campbell's team | Opens: pass; Can create: pass |\n| Travel booking portal | Flights and hotels through Northstar Travel | Exec vault in the password manager, Travel folder | Northstar Travel account manager | Opens: pass; Can create: fail (Can see bookings but not create them since the agency changed licences) |\n\n### Documents\n\n| Document | Type | Where | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Handover folder](https://drive.example.com/exec/handover-2026) | Folder |  | Final |\n| [One-page brief](https://drive.example.com/exec/handover-2026/brief) | One-page brief |  | Final |\n| [Principal profile](https://drive.example.com/exec/handover-2026/profile) | Principal profile |  | Final |\n| [Recording: preparing the board pack](https://drive.example.com/exec/handover-2026/board-pack-recording) | Recording |  | Final |\n| [Step guide: Thursday expense claims](https://drive.example.com/exec/handover-2026/expenses-guide) | Step guide |  | Final |\n| [Meeting request template for the chair](https://drive.example.com/exec/templates/chair-meeting-request) | Template |  | Final |\n| Personal contacts and travel documents list | Protected file | Locked drawer in Dana's office; Helen in HR holds the second key |  |\n| [Visa invitation letter](https://drive.example.com/exec/templates/visa-letter) | Other |  | Draft |"
    },
    {
      "id": "handover-knowledge",
      "title": "Rules, decisions and risks",
      "body": "### When this happens\n\n- If the chair's office calls, put them straight through to Dana, even in a meeting. (Board)\n- If a flight is cancelled while Dana is travelling, rebook the next flight in the same class first, then tell her. (Principal travelling)\n- If a meeting request mentions a journalist, decline politely and copy Communications.\n- If Dana can't be reached and something urgent arrives, call Ravi Campbell, then Joy Lindo. (Emergency plan)\n\n### Decisions\n\n| Date | Decision | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2026-03-02 | Fridays after 15:00 stay meeting-free | Dana uses the time to plan the week ahead. |\n| 2026-06-10 | Board packs go out through the portal only, never by email | A pack was forwarded by mistake in May. |\n| 2026-09-21 | Dana holds the diary herself from 26 September to 2 October | No overlap, and nobody else has delegate access. |\n\n### Risks\n\n| Risk | Kind | Severity | When |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Weekly expense claims miss Finance's Thursday cut-off | Recurring work | High | Every Thursday |\n| Board pack late or sent the wrong way | Occasional | High | Quarterly, the 7th of Mar, Jun, Sep and Dec |\n| AGM proxy forms not sent in time | Occasional | Medium | Every year, 15 May |\n| Only Priya knows how the chair likes meeting requests worded | Only one person knows | Medium |  |\n| Visa invitation letters for overseas guests | Occasional | Low | Rare |"
    },
    {
      "id": "handover-open",
      "title": "Open items",
      "body": "### In progress\n\n| What | Owner | Due |\n|---|---|---|\n| Book the venue for the Q4 leadership offsite | Marcus Hale | 2026-12-04 |\n| Renew the airline lounge memberships before they lapse | Marcus Hale | 2026-12-01 |\n\n### Gaps still open\n\n- **Blocks work:** Travel portal: Marcus can see bookings but not create them since the agency changed licences."
    },
    {
      "id": "handover-decide",
      "title": "Who decides what",
      "body": "| Decision | Who decides | Limit | Approver |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Accept or decline internal meeting requests | Decide alone |  |  |\n| Book travel and hotels | Decide alone | USD 2,000 |  |\n| Spend above USD 2,000 on travel or events | Check first |  | Ravi Campbell |\n| Gifts and hospitality for external guests | Check first | USD 250 | Dana Whitfield |\n| Anything involving the board chair | Always the principal |  |  |\n| Sign off the quarterly board budget | Always the principal |  | Dana Whitfield |"
    },
    {
      "id": "handover-plan",
      "title": "The handover plan",
      "body": "### Prepare\n\n| Step | Who | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Confirm the dates, track and folder link | Priya Nair | Done |\n| Do the eight-minute practice run first | Priya Nair | Not needed: Priya did the practice run when she set up an earlier handover. |\n| Run the day-one scoping session with the principal | Priya Nair | Done |\n| Answer: what breaks if Priya is not here on Monday? | Dana Whitfield | Done |\n| Draft the one-page brief and add its link | Priya Nair | Done |\n| List every system, where its credential lives and who grants access | Priya Nair | Done |\n| Answer the ask: Profile check | Dana Whitfield | Done |\n| Send the access approvals ask | Priya Nair | Done |\n| Give every thing in progress an actual completion date and an interim owner, must-haves first | Priya Nair | Done |\n| Answer the ask: Who decides what | Dana Whitfield | Done |\n| Hold the handback session with the principal | Priya Nair | Done |\n| Sign your part of the handover before you leave | Priya Nair | Done |\n\n### Incoming starts\n\n| Step | Who | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Run the access check on every system and link | Marcus Hale | Done |\n| Meet the three closest stakeholders | Marcus Hale | Done |\n\n### Incoming takes over\n\n| Step | Who | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Run the final check with the principal and record her verdict | Marcus Hale | Done |\n| Sign off | Marcus Hale | Done |\n| Answer the ask: Sign-off | Dana Whitfield | Done |\n\n### After\n\n| Step | Who | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Run the first follow-up check | Priya Nair | Done |\n| Run the second follow-up check | Priya Nair | Done |\n| 30-day check-in with the principal | Marcus Hale | Done |\n| 60-day check-in with the principal | Marcus Hale | Open |\n| 90-day check-in and handover notes review | Marcus Hale | Open |"
    }
  ],
  "plan": {
